@lang en
-- THIS FILE IS MEANT TO FAIL. Each assertion below states a WRONG expectation, so that the gate is shown to catch a wrong expectation.
-- check.sh lists this file with its exact count of failures (8) and encoding.json names it in `expected_red`.
-- Each wrong expectation is a tempting one:
--   the first day is left out of a period (s 18(h) says it is included);
--   an Act that says nothing is taken to come into operation only the day after its passing (s 16(1) says on the date of its passing);
--   a statutory instrument is taken to come into operation at the end of the day it is made (s 16(3) says the end of the day BEFORE);
--   a refusal is expected where the text does answer; a refusal is expected for the wrong reason;
--   "or" in s 12 is read as "and"; "made after that date" in s 18(b)(ii) is read as "on or after".
-- If one of these ever starts to pass, either the encoding has changed to follow the wrong reading, or the gate has stopped looking: both are findings.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ie-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `ie-general`
IMPORT `ie-operation-and-construction`

-- 1. s 18(h): the first day is included, so thirty days from 1 January end on 30 January, not 31 January.
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 30 `days beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2026 1 1) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 31

-- 2. s 16(1): an Act passed on 10 March 2026 that says nothing is in operation at the end of that day.
#ASSERT NOT `the enactment` (`Facts about an enactment` WITH `its kind` IS `an Act of the Oireachtas`, `what it says about commencement` IS `it says nothing about when it comes into operation`, `the day of its passing or making` IS JUST (YMD 2026 3 10)) `is in operation at the end of` (YMD 2026 3 10)

-- 3. s 16(3): an instrument made on 10 March 2026 that says nothing comes into operation at the end of 9 March, not of 10 March.
#ASSERT (`the moment at which the enactment comes into operation` (`Facts about an enactment` WITH `its kind` IS `a statutory instrument`, `what it says about commencement` IS `it says nothing about when it comes into operation`, `the day of its passing or making` IS JUST (YMD 2026 3 10)))'s `the day it ends` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 10

-- 4. s 18(b)(ii): "made after that date", so an instrument made on 22 December 1993 itself is not within it.
#ASSERT `a word importing the` feminine `gender is read as also importing the other gender in an enactment of kind` `a statutory instrument` `passed or made on` (YMD 1993 12 22)

-- 5. s 18(h) with Sch Pt 1 "month": one calendar month from 1 February 2025 is determinate (28 February), so a refusal is the wrong expectation.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of` 1 `calendar months beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2025 2 1)

-- 6. s 18(h): the refusal for a period of years is for a start that is not 1 January, not for a period "after an event".
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of` 3 `years beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2025 7 16) BECAUSE "section 18(h) says nothing about a period counted after an event"

-- 7. s 12: "does not materially affect the substance of the form OR is not misleading": a form that fails both is not saved.
#ASSERT `section 12 saves the form used` TRUE FALSE FALSE

-- 8. s 21(2): an instrument that comes into operation at the same moment as this Act does not come into operation AFTER it.
#ASSERT `Part 2 of the Schedule applies to the enactment` (`Facts about an enactment` WITH `its kind` IS `a statutory instrument`, `what it says about commencement` IS `it is expressed to come into operation on a particular day` (YMD 2006 1 1), `the day of its passing or making` IS JUST (YMD 2005 12 1))
